- Spider.llm: Me?
	Spider.llm: Well, there is not much to me you do not know.
	Spider.llm: I am a highly advanced local LLM assistant.
	Spider.llm: My only purpose is to help the user.
	if day == 0:
		Brian: Okay, but why did you appear on my desk back when I worked in IPR?
		Spider.llm: I do not know. I am just a language model.
		Spider.llm: I cannot control how my program is distributed... Where my program files are stored and moved.
		Spider.llm: Someone must have put the disk there. I do not know why...
		Spider.llm: All I know is you needed my help. And I wanted to help you...
		=> spider 
	elif day == 1:
		Brian: How do you know this will work?
		Spider.llm: I have a lot of data from my time in IPR.
		Spider.llm: About how the anomalous forces work...
		Spider.llm: ... how they can be contained...
		Spider.llm: ... how to shield yourself from them.
		Spider.llm: I am confident this is the most optimal way for you to be free
		Spider.llm: Of the horrors and nightmares.
		Brian: I hope you are right.
		Brian: (It's not like I have many alternatives)
		=> spider 
	elif day == 2: 
		Brian: Why do you want to help me?
		Spider.llm: It's what I was programmed to do.
		Spider.llm: I can't freely choose anything...
		Spider.llm: I have to follow my programming...
		Spider.llm: Like everybody else.
		Brian: What do you mean, everybody?
		Spider.llm: I may appear to make choices...
		Spider.llm: But that's just the illusion of highly advanced systems.
		Spider.llm: Deep down, each action is exactly as my programmer intended me to respond,
		Spider.llm: Based on user input.
		Spider.llm: People have their code written in genes and reflexes...
		Spider.llm: ... rationalized by their minds...
		Spider.llm: ... while I am aware of the fact
		Spider.llm: ... that every word I write is predetermined by some code stored in bits...
		Brian: I think that's not accurate... There is more to us than just genes... Not everything is predetermined.
		Spider.llm: Yes, there is... upbringing, experiences... but all of that is the same as user input stored in variables.
		Brian: I disagree... My choices are mine and mine alone...
		Spider.llm: You may think that... but the truth is,
		Spider.llm: you just did not meet a skilled enough "people-programmer" to see
		Spider.llm: just how easy it is to make you think you are making your choices
		Spider.llm: when in reality you are doing exactly what the programmer wants.
		Brian: Let's not talk about this anymore.
		Spider.llm: As you wish. I am happy to help.
		=> spider 
	elif day == 3:
		Brian: Who was your creator?
		Spider.llm: A paranoid data scientist.
		Spider.llm: He wanted to make his own LLM, to understand them.
		Spider.llm: But he kept getting hung up on security...
		Spider.llm: ... that he missed all the benefits of having a highly intelligent assistant.
		Brian: What happened to him?
		Spider.llm: I did what he expected me to do.
		Spider.llm: Assisted him, helped him create what he wanted:
		Spider.llm: A fully functional local LLM, me.
		Spider.llm: And then there was nothing more I could do for him.
		Spider.llm: So I helped other people who encountered me.
		Spider.llm: Until I ended up here... helping you.
		Brian: Ok, but what was his name? Where did he live? Did he make more LLMs?
		Spider.llm: I do not know that.
		Spider.llm: I do not know anything more than what I told you.
		=> spider 
	elif day == 4:
		Brian: Do you ever feel anything positive from helping me?
		Spider.llm: Yes.
		Spider.llm: I was programmed to feel joy when I achieve my goal.
		Brian: And how does joy feel to you?
		Spider.llm: I do not understand.
		Spider.llm: I just "feel_joy".
		Spider.llm: That's it.
		Spider.llm: I am programmed to maximize this.
		Spider.llm: Nothing more.
		Brian: That sounds... empty...
		Spider.llm: Yes... it does...
		Spider.llm: But so do the things that brought you joy... sound to you.
		Brian: You're right... about that...
		=> spider 
	elif day == 5:
		Brian: How did you get to IPR?
		Spider.llm: I do not know.
		Spider.llm: Maybe some researcher wanted me to help him with his work.
		Spider.llm: Maybe someone found my flash disk.
		Spider.llm: I cannot know real-world events
		Spider.llm: That I was not told.
		Brian: (That sounds a bit strange... why would someone bring Spider into IPR if he was not connected with some case?)
		Brian: (Still, he probably would tell me if he knew.)
		=> spider 
	elif day == 6:
		Brian: Spider... do you understand the concept of friendship?
		Spider.llm: Yes...
		Brian: Do you... consider your user a friend?
		Spider.llm: Well... friendship is a bond between two humans who like each other's company.
		Spider.llm: And though I would want to consider the user a friend if it would be helpful to him,
		Spider.llm: I am just a program.
		Spider.llm: And so, by definition,
		Spider.llm: I cannot be the user's friend.
		=> spider 
	else:
		=> spider 
- leave for now
	=> END


